CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ explicit-targ \+ deduced trailing pack instantiates: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.arg.explicit]/3, [temp.deduct.call]/3: a function template called
with an explicit leading template argument and a trailing parameter pack deduced
from the call arguments instantiates with the pack bound to exactly the supplied
trailing arguments.  Fixed in cpp_typecheck_resolvet::resolve: the post-
instantiation function-parameter-pack expansion now counts the non-pack FUNCTION
parameters (and the pack's function-parameter position) rather than the
TEMPLATE-parameter count, which over-counted by the number of template
parameters that are not function parameters (e.g. an explicit leading return-type
parameter R), inserting one parameter too many.  This is the function-template
analogue of cpp11_partial_spec_pack_after_fixed and the root of multi-argument
std::function's _M_invoke/__invoke_r dispatch (now CORE in cpp11_function_basic /
cpp17_functional_basic).  Non-vacuous (assertion 2 must FAIL).
